  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Write 170 as the sum of the smallest possible number of square numbers without using $1^2=1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$170=7^2+11^2$; two square numbers.\n\nSince $13^2<170<14^2$, one square number cannot suffice.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}7^2+11^2&=49+121\\\\7^2+11^2&=170\\end{align*}$$\n\nNeither square is $1^2$. Also, $13^2=169$ and $14^2=196$, so $170$ is not itself a square number. Therefore the smallest possible number of square numbers is two.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
